insert into public.kb_articles (slug, title, content, category) values
  ($kb$about-tricore$kb$, $kb$About Tricore IT Solutions$kb$, $kb$Tricore IT Solutions is an online store for IT products. Customers browse the catalog, choose a product, enter their delivery address and place the order; the item is reserved for them. After placing the order, a support ticket is opened automatically and our team contacts the customer to confirm the order and arrange payment and delivery. There is no online payment gateway. The order is then shipped to the customer's address, and the customer can follow every step, including the courier and tracking number, under My orders. Product categories shown on the website are: Laptops and Desktops, Networking, Servers and Storage, Security and CCTV, Peripherals, and Software and Licenses. The exact products, prices and stock that are currently available are listed in the PRODUCTS section of the context.$kb$, $kb$core$kb$),
  ($kb$how-ordering-works$kb$, $kb$How ordering works$kb$, $kb$Step 1: Sign in with your Google account and open the Shop. Step 2: Click Buy on a product, which opens the checkout page. Step 3: Enter your delivery address (name, phone number, PIN code and address) and place the order; the item is reserved for you. Step 4: A support ticket is opened automatically and our team contacts you through it to confirm the order and arrange payment and delivery. Step 5: Payment and delivery are handled directly with our team - there is no online payment gateway. Step 6: The order is shipped to your address and the courier name and tracking number appear under My orders. Step 7: The order is marked delivered. The assistant in the chat can start an order for you, but the address and confirmation are completed on the checkout page.$kb$, $kb$core$kb$),
  ($kb$talk-to-human$kb$, $kb$Prices, special deals and the Tricore team$kb$, $kb$The assistant cannot change prices, give discounts or coupons, approve special or bulk deals, or create custom quotes. If a customer wants a lower price or a special deal, the assistant explains it cannot do that itself and asks whether the customer would like to be connected with the Tricore team. Orders are confirmed through a support ticket: after placing an order, our team contacts the customer to arrange payment and delivery. There is no online payment gateway. Exact delivery times, shipping charges, returns and warranty terms are not listed here, so the assistant must say honestly that it does not have them on hand and must not guess.$kb$, $kb$core$kb$),
  ($kb$sign-in$kb$, $kb$Signing in and creating an account$kb$, $kb$Tricore uses Google sign-in only. There is no separate password. New customers create their account by clicking Sign up with Google, and returning customers click Sign in with Google. You must be signed in to open the Shop and to see your orders. The landing page and this assistant are available without signing in.$kb$, $kb$general$kb$),
  ($kb$order-status$kb$, $kb$Order status meanings$kb$, $kb$After signing in, customers can see all their orders under My orders with a step-by-step progress bar. The status meanings are: Awaiting payment means the order is placed and our team will contact you through a support ticket to arrange payment and delivery. Payment received means payment is confirmed and the order will be shipped. Shipped means the order was dispatched and the courier name and tracking number are shown. Delivered means the order reached the customer. Cancelled means the order was cancelled. A customer can cancel their own order while it is still awaiting payment.$kb$, $kb$general$kb$),
  ($kb$products-and-stock$kb$, $kb$Products, prices and availability$kb$, $kb$Products, prices and availability are shown in the Shop and in the PRODUCTS section of the context. Prices are in Indian rupees. A product marked out of stock cannot be ordered. Low stock means only a few units are left. The item is reserved when an order is placed, and is returned to stock if the order is cancelled.$kb$, $kb$general$kb$)
